# Title: Invoke-Obfuscation Obfuscated IEX Invocation
# ID: 4bf943c6-5146-4273-98dd-e958fd1e3abf
# Status: test
# Level: high
# Author: Daniel Bohannon (@Mandiant/@FireEye), oscd.community
# Date: 2019-11-08
# Tags: attack.stealth, attack.t1027, attack.execution, attack.t1059.001
# Description: Detects all variations of obfuscated powershell IEX invocation code generated by Invoke-Obfuscation framework from the following code block
# Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

index=* eventtype=wineventlog ((regex process_exec="(?i)\\$PSHome\\[\\s*\\d{1,3}\\s*\\]\\s*\\+\\s*\\$PSHome\\[") OR (regex process_exec="(?i)\\$ShellId\\[\\s*\\d{1,3}\\s*\\]\\s*\\+\\s*\\$ShellId\\[") OR (regex process_exec="(?i)\\$env:Public\\[\\s*\\d{1,3}\\s*\\]\\s*\\+\\s*\\$env:Public\\[") OR (regex process_exec="(?i)\\$env:ComSpec\\[(?:\\s*\\d{1,3}\\s*,){2}") OR (regex process_exec="(?i)\\*mdr\\*\\W\\s*\\)\\.Name") OR (regex process_exec="(?i)\\$VerbosePreference\\.ToString\\(") OR (regex process_exec="(?i)\\[String\\]\\s*\\$VerbosePreference"))
